2. FFmpeg (GPL)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The image contains a minimal build of FFmpeg, built with libx264 and therefore
licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later. FFmpeg is a
separate program that the plugin starts as a child process; the plugin's own
code is not linked into it.

This NOTICE and the files in /usr/share/licenses/ in the image are the GPL
notices for the GPL components of the image: the license texts of FFmpeg
(COPYING.GPLv2, COPYING.GPLv3, LICENSE.md) are in /usr/share/licenses/ffmpeg/,
the license of this plugin in /usr/share/licenses/capture-plugin/.

GPL components and where to get their source code:

- FFmpeg: the file /usr/share/licenses/ffmpeg/SOURCE names the exact version,
  the download location of the corresponding source code
  (https://ffmpeg.org/releases/), its SHA-256 and the configure line. The build
  recipe is the Dockerfile in this repository (stage ffmpeg-builder).
- libx264: the Debian package libx264-164 (source package x264), installed from
  Debian trixie. The same SOURCE file lists the exact package version and its
  source package version, written when the image was built. The corresponding
  source code is at https://sources.debian.org/src/x264/ and
  https://tracker.debian.org/pkg/x264, or with `apt-get source x264=<version>`.
- Avahi client libraries (libavahi-client3, libavahi-common3, LGPL): Debian
  source package avahi, https://tracker.debian.org/pkg/avahi, version in SOURCE.

Written offer: if you cannot obtain the corresponding source code of any of
